  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information is the pairwise differences in outcomes between Lottery A and Lottery B. Lottery A has outcomes of 2500€ (33%), 2400€ (66%), and 0€ (1%). Lottery B has a single outcome of 2400€ (100%). The pairwise outcome differences are computed as follows: (2500 - 2400) = +100€ (when A yields 2500 and B yields 2400), (2400 - 2400) = 0€ (when A yields 2400 and B yields 2400), and (0 - 2400) = -2400€ (when A yields 0 and B yields 2400). The sum of these differences, weighted or unweighted, involves comparing how much better or worse A is than B across all outcome pairs. The reason prefers the lottery for which the sum of pairwise outcome differences is more favorable (i.e., higher). While the exact aggregation method (e.g., expected difference, simple sum) is not specified, the information needed—outcome levels in both lotteries—is available.",
