  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the sum of all pairwise outcome differences between the two lotteries and preferring the one with the more favorable sum. However, the individual does not consider all pairwise differences; they ignore the 0€ outcome in A due to its low probability and focus only on the favorable difference (2500 vs 2400). They do not mention or imply a comprehensive comparison of all outcome pairs or an aggregation of differences. Their justification is based on a selective, non-systematic comparison favoring the best-case gain, rather than a structured evaluation of all outcome differences. Therefore, while outcome differences are loosely referenced, the full scope of the decision reason—considering all pairwise differences and summing them—is not reflected in the report. The reasoning style is more consistent with a 'best-outcome' heuristic than the specified pairwise difference summation rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
